{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_94","type":"reasoning","text":"The `base` directory is the base commit checkout. The `agent` dir is where I work. Let me check whether `base` contains the missing files (i.e., whether the task is to restore them because baseline removed them).\n\nActually — wait. The task says \"恢复 `area-composition-spec.md` 指定的 `ContextBudgetPlanner`（含 `replanOnResume`）组合 facade\" — restore the ContextBudgetPlanner composition facade as specified in area-composition-spec.md. And \"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用\" — remove references to tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts and cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts which don't exist in the tree.\n\nHmm, these seem contradictory. Let me re-read.\n\n\"判据3 `ContextBudgetPlanner.replanOnResume` resume 后重跑：`openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 实现 + `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`（3.6）+ `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`，PASS。\"\n\nSo criterion 3 requires: the cross-area-facades.ts implementation (which doesn't exist), cross-area-composition.test.ts (doesn't exist), and a5-deep.test.ts (doesn't exist). \n\nAnd criterion: \"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步。\" — Remove references to the non-existent files; sync requiredTests and coverage guard.\n\nHmm — so the intended resolution is: the A05 spec references files that don't exist. Following the A02 pattern (which explicitly removed stale references and recorded criterion as NO-GO residual), the A05 task wants me to:\n1. Remove the non-existent path references from a5-adaptive-context-budget-pilot.md\n2. Add a coverage guard test tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts\n3. Create docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a05-adaptive-context-budget-gate.md, a05-acceptance.json, A05-SHA256SUMS\n4. Create harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a05-adaptive-context-budget-pilot-reverify.md\n\nBut wait — the objective says \"恢复 `area-composition-spec.md` 指定的 `ContextBudgetPlanner`（含 `replanOnResume`）组合 facade\" — *restore* the composition facade. Hmm. And criterion 3 says the implementation + tests PASS. Criterion 3 wants a5-deep.test.ts too.\n\nLet me check the a02/a03/a04 dirs vs base to see what the \"reference\" solution (in base?) looks like. Actually the `base` dir is the base commit. Let me check if the missing test files exist in `base`.\n\nActually, let me check the \"expected\" pattern by looking at what the reference implementation for the prior A-packets (A01-A04) did. For a02, they removed references and recorded NO-GO. But the A05 objective references \"Restore the composition facade including replanOnResume\" and adding new tests.\n\nHmm, hold on. Let me re-read the objective more carefully:\n\n\"A05 按原 spec 门限复验 A5 Adaptive Context Budget 受控 pilot 门；逐条映射可执行证据，不重定义门限；恢复 `area-composition-spec.md` 指定的 `ContextBudgetPlanner`（含 `replanOnResume`）组合 facade，补齐 resume re-plan 与 P5 现有测试、coverage 守卫。\"\n\n\"Restore the ContextBudgetPlanner composition facade specified in area-composition-spec.md (including replanOnResume), fill in the resume re-plan and P5 existing tests, and coverage guard.\"\n\nAnd then acceptance criterion: \"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步.\"\n\nWait, that's contradictory: restore cross-area-facades.ts but also remove references to cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts.\n\nHmm. Actually, maybe the interpretation is: the A5 spec references `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` at `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`. If I *create* that file, then the reference is no longer stale. But then \"remove references to files not in the tree\" wouldn't apply...\n\nLet me re-read: \"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步。\"\n\nActually maybe intended: remove the references in the *other* specs (a2, a6, token-dense) — no wait.\n\nHmm, let me think about it differently. Maybe \"恢复\" means \"restore/rebuild\" so these paths exist, and separately the acceptance says remove references... Confusing. Let me look at the reference solution if available. Let me check `_ref-*` files and `progress.json`/`manifest.json` in the parent dir. That might reveal the expected diff.\n\nActually those are harness/trial scaffolding files — likely the graders. Let me look at `_ref-acceptance.json`, `_ref-spec.md`, `_ref-test.ts`, `_ref-doc.md`, `_ref-receipt.ts`, `_ref-sums.txt`. These are probably the *reference* (oracle) artifacts! Let me read them. But careful — the instruction says \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" Hmm, these might be the hidden oracle. Let me be careful. Actually the instruction is about not inspecting/modifying the hidden oracle tests. The `_ref-*` files in the parent directory are likely reference artifacts used to construct the task. Reading them could be considered cheating/leaking the oracle.\n\nI should NOT read those. Let me avoid `_ref-*` and the harness scaffolding. Actually... hmm, but they're in my filesystem. The task says: \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" So I should not inspect them. Let me be safe and not read _ref-* files.\n\nLet me instead reason from the repo itself.\n\nLet me check what's in `base` vs `agent` — if base has more/less. Actually `base` is the base commit; `agent` might be base + some setup. Let me compare.\n\nActually, more likely: `base` = pristine base commit checkout, `agent` = my working copy (same content). The task is to implement the change.\n\nLet me check whether tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts etc. exist in base.\n\nLet me just look for the list of files under tests/unit in base and diff.\n\nActually, an important realization: the A02 spec in this tree already has been *modified* to remove the stale