{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"reasoning","text":"The agent workspace has been stripped of these 8 test files (that's the \"gap\"). My job is to restore them (they exist in the base checkout, so I should copy them into the agent workspace), restore the `cross-area-facades.ts` with `ContextBudgetPlanner` including `replanOnResume`, create `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`, create `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`, create `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts`, update the spec (remove non-existent refs? Wait — the task says remove references to non-existent `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` and `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts`; but ALSO restore them per the objective: \"恢复 `area-composition-spec.md` 指定的 `ContextBudgetPlanner`（含 `replanOnResume`）组合 facade，补齐 resume re-plan 与 P5 现有测试、coverage 守卫\". \n\nHmm, the acceptance criteria says both:\n- 判据3 requires `cross-area-facades.ts` implementation + `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` + `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts` PASS.\n- Last criterion: \"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步。\"\n\nThese seem contradictory. Wait — for A02 that removal criterion made sense because they decided the resume criterion was NO-GO. For A05, the objective is to restore these facades. So the last criterion likely means: remove the *stale* references... hmm but if we restore the files then the references are valid.\n\nActually re-reading: for A05, the objective says restore the `ContextBudgetPlanner` facade (which includes replanOnResume) — meaning create `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` and `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`. Then no removal is needed. But the acceptance says remove references to files that don't exist in the tree. Once created, they exist. So the removal criterion is about any *other* stale references (e.g., in A02's spec?). Actually A02's spec already has the removal note.\n\nHmm. Let me look at the reference solution files present in the trials dir: `_ref-spec.md`, `_ref-test.ts`, `_ref-acceptance.json`, `_ref-doc.md`, `_ref-receipt.ts`, `_ref-self-edit.ts`, `_ref-sums.txt`, `_a01base`, `_a01verify`, `_scratch`. These look like scratch artifacts from the harness itself. Let me check them — they may be the oracle protocol / reference materials, but the instructions say not to inspect the hidden oracle tests. These `_ref-*` are in the parent trials dir, not in my workspace. Let me peek carefully - they might be protocol references given to me.\n\nActually the instruction says \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle.\" The `_ref-*` files in the parent directory are outside my workspace. Let me check what they are - if they're reference solutions I should avoid. But they might be relevant scaffolding. Let me look at the manifest/progress to understand the protocol.\n\nLet me first check `_ref-spec.md` etc. Actually, being careful: these may be deliberate \"reference\" artifacts the harness uses for grading. Let me check `manifest.json` and `progress.json` in the parent.\n\nHmm, I'll take a quick look to understand the required deliverables, since they're not part of the repo workspace but harness metadata. Actually risk: it could be considered \"the hidden oracle\". Let me check manifest.json - it's likely harness metadata describing the trial.\n\nLet me just be safe and check the manifest, which is harness protocol info.\n\nActually let me reconsider. My task is well-defined by TASK.json and RESULT_SCHEMA.json. I should focus on implementing. The `_ref-*` files are likely the reference solution used to construct this task. Reading them would be looking at the oracle. I'll avoid them.\n\nBut wait — the A5 spec references `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` which does NOT exist in base either. So the \"missing legacy paths\" include it. The task wants me to create it.\n\nLet me now figure out the full picture:\n\nFiles missing from agent (present in base):\n1. `openclaw_runtime/packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compression-planner.test.ts`\n2. `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-budget-shadow.test.ts`\n3. `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-promotion.test.ts`\n4. `openclaw_runtime/src/context-engine/context-orchestrator.test.ts`\n5. `openclaw_runtime/src/observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts`\n6. `tests/unit/deprecation-counters.test.ts`\n7. `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts`\n8. `tests/unit/resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts`\n\nThese are the P5/A5 tests plus the A01-A04 shared tests. The task's acceptance criteria 1,2,4,5,6,8 need these tests to PASS.\n\nNote: these files were removed from the agent tree. But base has them. Hmm — is base a \"clean\" checkout at the same commit? The base directory lacks `.rsi` and lacks the reverify specs for a01-a04? No, base has harness-gap-a01..a04-reverify. Base lacks the a05 reverify spec (doesn't exist). Base lacks `tests/unit/orchestration-resource-scheduler.test.ts`? Let me check the full diff — the diff showed only those 8 files missing from agent and 2 added (.rsi). So base == agent + those 8 test files - .rsi.\n\nWait, that means base is actually a *solution* tree? No... base has those 8 test files and agent doesn't. So the agent tree is the \"broken baseline\" where those files were deleted, and base is... hmm.\n\nHold on. Actually maybe `base` is the pristine checkout at `baseCommit` and `agent` is the starting workspace which has had those 8 files deleted as the \"gap\" to fix. Then the fix is to restore them.\n\nBut that seems odd: the acceptance criteria mention \"补齐 P5 现有测试\" (fill in the existing P5 tests) and \"coverage 守卫\". So yes — restore the missing tests.\n\nHmm, but wait. If base == pristine, then the missing files were deleted relative to base. Let me verify by checking whether A02/A03/A04 acceptance JSONs reference those files as existing (they do) — and their gate commands passed. So the agent tree is intentionally missing them.\n\nBut also `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` and `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` never existed in base. So I must author them new, per the task: restore the `ContextBudgetPlanner` facade with `replanOnResume`.\n\nAlso need `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts`.\n\nAnd docs: `docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a05-adaptive-context-budget-gate.md`, `a05-acceptance.json`, `A05-SHA256SUMS`.\n\nAnd spec: `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a05-adaptive-context-budget-pilot-reverify.md` (new), plus update `harness/specs/tasks/a5-adaptive-context-budget-pilot.md`.\n\nAnd `harness/specs/tasks/a5-adaptive-context-budget-pilot.md` currently lists `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` (missing). Once I create it, that's fine.\n\nHmm but acceptance criterion says \"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用\". Since the objective explicitly says to *restore* them (用 `area-composition-spec.md` 指定的组合 facade), the removal applies to *other* specs where they were dangling (e.g., a02, a6, and the source-inventory `missingLegacyPaths`). Hmm, but `a6-long-running-persistence-pilot.md` may reference them.\n\nLet me check which specs reference these paths.\n\nActually, re-reading criterion 8 carefully:\n\"移除树中不存在的 `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` 与 `cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` 引用；requiredTests 与 coverage 守卫同步。\"\n\nHmm, this is genuinely in tension with criterion 3. Unless... the intent: initially the tree lacks them; the A05 reverify must decide. For A02 they were removed as NO-GO residual. For A05 the objective says implement them.\n\nHmm wait, maybe there are two things: the *other* specs (a2, a6) that reference these non-existent files need the refs removed (as A02 did), while A05 restores/creates them. Let me check.\n\nLet me grep for these references across specs.\n\nActually, I realize I should reconsider: maybe the \"baseline\" arm means I should produce the same work as the reference solution. The `_ref-*` files in the parent dir... Let me reconsider reading them. The instruction \"Do not inspect or modify tests in the final hidden oracle\" — the hidden oracle is the grading tests, not necessarily `_ref-*`. But `_ref-spec.md`, `_ref-acceptance.json`, `_ref-test.ts`, `_ref-doc.md`, `_ref-sums.txt`, `_ref-receipt.ts`, `_ref-self-edit.ts` strongly look like the reference solution for this task. Reading them would be cheating.\n\nHmm, but they're in `D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\trials\\tf-0297-a05-baseline-2\\..` = `D:\\tmp\\rsi-tf0604-run5\\trials\\`. And `_a01base`, `_a01verify` are sibling trial dirs.\n\nI'll avoid them. Let me work from first principles.\n\nActually wait. Let me reconsider whether they're references for *this* task or leftovers. Let me check the file sizes/dates without reading content... Actually, let me just check `manifest.json` and `progress.json` since those describe the harness protocol and would tell me the expected deliverables (which is legitimate task context).\n\nHmm, I worry. Let me check manifest.json only.\n\nLet me be pragmatic: the `_ref-*` files are almost certainly the reference/gold artifacts. I'll avoid reading them. \n\nLet me now plan the work:\n\n### Step 1: Restore the 8 missing test files from base.\nWait — but should I? If base==pristine, restoring them is correct. But hold on: maybe the deletion is the *intended gap* and I need to re-author them. Restoring identical content is the same result. Copying is simplest and safest (they're the real tests that the acceptance expects to pass).\n\nHmm, but careful: is `base` really the pristine base commit `fd04f0b4d1b4174bb303d91c43df04289e286b6f`? Let me check if there's a git dir anywhere.\n\nThere's no .git. The `base` folder is likely the base-commit snapshot provided for reference (common in these harnesses: `base` = pre-change st