{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_159","type":"command_execution","command":"\"D:\\\\software\\\\PowerShell\\\\pwsh-7.6.6\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'rg -n \"buildCompactionBudgetShadow|recordSafeguardBudgetShadow|recordEmbeddedCompactionBudgetCounters|buildDeterministicCompressionArtifact|TierSchedule|tierSchedule|normalizeTierSchedule\" --hidden -g \"!.git\" -g \"!node_modules\" | Out-String -Width 250'","aggregated_output":"docs\\clawx-design-overview.md:784:- **Token-dense artifact**: compaction stores a structured `CompressionArtifact v1` with objective, constraints, current state, done/in-progress/blocked work, decisions, files/tests, failed attempts, deviations, next action, review items, evidence refs, unverified claims, and quality metrics. v1 also carries an optional bounded `semanticAtoms` ledger (goal, latest user ask, decision, constraint, failed attempt, entity, next action, outcome, safety boundary) whose critical atoms must have evidence refs; unverified/stale/superseded/conflict states stay visible, and consecutive compactions preserve the previous artifact lineage instead of deleting superseded atoms. Provider, built-in LLM, and boundary compaction outputs all pass through the same finalize pipeline (normalize -> artifact -> critical ledger comparison -> damage audit -> shadow decision), so `details.artifact` and `details.validatedPipeline` are written on every safeguard exit while `wouldRetry` / `wouldFallback` / `wouldPreserveTurns` remain shadow-only diagnostics. P3 adds deterministic addressability: `auditCompactionAddressability` requires every critical atom to resolve to an archive handle, file hunk, or CVK selector, `bindCompactionArchiveEvidence` writes the checkpoint archive handle into critical atom evidence refs before checkpoint persist, and the next compaction uses `buildPreviousCompactionLedgerMessage` so atom-ledger + new messages are re-distilled instead of recursively summarizing the previous natural-language summary. The old string `summary` is rendered from the artifact as a projection for compatibility; recovery paths should prefer the artifact projection over re-reading long transcript history. P5 keeps the production 0.6/0.75/0.85/0.95 ladder as the hard backstop while allowing optional per-task-class `thresholds`/`tierSchedule` that can only move compaction earlier; `planCriticalFirstBudget` fixes the critical-ledger-first shadow budget order, real embedded-compaction and safeguard call sites write the A5 deprecation counters, and `budgetShadow` stays diagnostics-only on `CompactionDetails` (never in `CompressionArtifact`). Model declarations `nativeMemory`/`nativeContextGating` additively negotiate memory_pilot/vtoken/BlockStore injection off through the Context Orchestrator with provenance receipts; no declaration leaves behavior unchanged. P6 adds the fixed promotion order (`shadow -> would-retry -> provider-pressure-pilot -> critical-only -> limited`) with a pure promotion gate evaluator; the runtime `agents.defaults.compaction.promotionStage` defaults to `shadow`, provider would-retry is bounded, and critical-only/limited fail closed by cancelling a compaction that would preserve critical turns. Promotion to higher stages still requires the P6 evidence gates and is not implied by this development work.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:97:                       │                   tierSchedule,       │              │\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:107:                 │ ◄─ tierSchedule    │   │   registry     │  │\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:130:Data flow: prompt + cheap stats → classification → plan. In **shadow** mode the plan flows only into the evaluator (predictions recorded next to actuals; zero behavior change). In **pilot/active** mode, two additive consumption points activate: (a) `tierSchedule` supplies per-task-class soft thresholds to the existing tier selector — which may only move thresholds EARLIER (lower), so the production ladder remains the hard backstop; (b) `providerPriorities` + provider `budgetHints` shape assemble-stage allocation. Artifact `quality` flows back into the cost model, closing the loop.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:187:export type TierSchedule = {\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:190:   * INVARIANT enforced by normalizeTierSchedule: every scheduled threshold must be\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:197:export function normalizeTierSchedule(input?: Partial<TierThresholds>): TierSchedule;\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:202:**Error handling.** `normalizeTierSchedule` clamps: non-finite/out-of-range values fall back to the default for that tier; a schedule that violates monotonicity (`tier1 < tier2 < tier3 < tier4`) is rejected wholesale to defaults with a warning string that flows into `CompressionTelemetry.warnings`.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:221:  tierSchedule: TierSchedule;\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:335:| `packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compression-planner.ts` (production) | **Additive param:** `selectCompressionPlan` gains optional `thresholds?: TierThresholds`; `CompressionPlannerInput` gains optional `tierSchedule?: TierSchedule`. Absent → literals behave exactly as today (0.6/0.75/0.85/0.95). | The single point where per-task-class scheduling meets the production ladder; parameterize, don't fork. |\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:336:| `packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/budget-schedule.ts` (NEW) | New pure module: `DEFAULT_TIER_THRESHOLDS`, `TierSchedule`, `normalizeTierSchedule` with the ≤-defaults invariant. | Names the currently-inline thresholds once; the ≤ invariant makes \"earlier only\" mechanically enforced. |\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:337:| `packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compaction.ts` (production, ~29 KB) | **Additive:** `CompactionSettings` gains optional `tierSchedule?: TierSchedule`; threaded into the two `planCompression` call sites (compaction.ts:792, compaction.ts:801). `CompactionDetails` gains optional `budgetShadow?`. | Settings already flow here; two optional-field additions, no control-flow change when absent. |\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:358:3. **Planning.** `planContextBudget` (`budget-planner-shadow.ts`) consults the `CompressionCostModel`: history slices for (`refactor`, `tier1`) show median `quality.score` 0.78, `lowLevelShare` 0.05 → `expectedQualityRisk` low; `savedInputTokens` over ~30 remaining turns dwarfs `redistillationCost` → net-positive. Plan: `budgetTokens` = window, `reserveRatio` honoring `MIN_PROMPT_BUDGET_TOKENS`/`MIN_PROMPT_BUDGET_RATIO` and `CompactionSettings.reserveTokens` (default 16384), `tierSchedule` = refactor row (tier1 at **0.50** instead of the production-reactive 0.75), `providerPriorities` marking memory/loop-pack providers `supporting` and opportunistic retrieval `opportunistic`, plus a predicted pressure curve.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:360:5. **Planned early firing.** At turn 19 pressure reaches 0.52. The runner's compaction path passes `settings.tierSchedule` through `prepareCompaction` → `planCompression` (compaction.ts:792). Inside, `selectCompressionPlan(..., thresholds)` now returns `{ tier: \"tier1\", strategy: \"micro-compact\", pressure: 0.52 }` — under production defaults this would still be `tier0`/`hot-context`. `planCompression` micro-compacts messages ≥ 1200 chars (stack-trace/tool-output/file-body compactors), leaving the hot tail intact. The production ladder is still armed above: if the plan mispredicts and pressure later hits 0.95, `emergency-collapse` fires exactly as today.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:361:6. **Artifact + persistence.** `buildDeterministicCompressionArtifact` (`compression-artifact.ts`) builds the v1 artifact; `buildQuality` computes `{ score: 0.81, level: \"medium\", fieldCoverage, evidenceCoverage, artifactTokens, projectionTokens, warnings }`. The harness persists `CompactionDetails { readFiles, modifiedFiles, compression, artifact, budgetShadow }` — the last field being the new additive record with the plan, curve error so far, and this firing.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:370:**Operator gate.** One config knob, default off: `agents.defaults.contextBudget.mode: \"off\" | \"shadow\" | \"pilot\" | \"active\"` (resolved through the same config path as `agents.defaults.bootstrapMaxChars`; flag reader added beside `shadow-flags.ts`). Optional per-class overrides `agents.defaults.contextBudget.classes.<taskClass>.tier1..tier4`, clamped by `normalizeTierSchedule`.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:372:**Phase 0 — off (default).** No classification, no planning, no recording. Flag-off parity: `selectCompressionPlan` receives no thresholds and reproduces 0.6/0.75/0.85/0.95 exactly; `CompactionSettings.tierSchedule` is absent; zero new fields written.\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:374:**Phase 1 — shadow (ADVISORY_ONLY).** Classifier + planner + cost model + evaluator run; `tierSchedule` and `providerPriorities` are computed but consumed by NOBODY in the execution path. Records written: `budgetShadow` on compaction entries, session rollup diagnostics. Duration: until gates below have data (≥ 20 sessions, ≥ 10 containing at least one real compression event — personal-machine scale).\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:383:**Phase 2 — pilot.** `tierSchedule` becomes live at the two `planCompression` call sites. Provider `budgetHints` remain out of scope until a separate formal provider-runtime spec defines their production owner and gate. Shadow recording continues (now predicted-vs-actual-with-intervention). Promotion gates pilot → active:\r\ndocs\\enhancements\\05-adaptive-context-budget.md:410