orded as an oracle write (i.e., the grader overwrote it with the frozen version). And the a01 trial failed because the frozen guard test + tool-registration test failed — the agent's production changes didn't match.\n\nSo: the critical work is to make the *production code* satisfy the frozen tests. The frozen tests are the 8 files present in the `base` checkout (which is the base commit, not necessarily the reference solution). Wait — base is the base commit fd04f0b4. Let me check: does the base checkout contain the *frozen* test files? The oracle digests: let me verify by hashing the base checkout's copies.\n\nLet me hash `D:\\...\\base\\tests\\unit\\resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts` and compare with the manifest digest 7183a6dc...\n\nAlso need `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts` — not in base. That one is the hidden signal path; likely the grader will use the *agent's own* file? No... Let me check: for a01, `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` exists in both base and agent. Let me hash base's a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts.\n\nHmm, actually in a01's case, `tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts` is listed in *both* scrubbedOraclePaths and oracleWrites? Let me re-read: a01 result has `oracleWrites: [\"tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts\"]` and `scrubbedOraclePaths` doesn't include it, `preexistingOraclePaths` doesn't include it. So a01's guard test was NOT scrubbed from the agent workspace and NOT preexisting — meaning the agent created it, and it was recorded as an \"oracle write\".\n\nHmm, that's confusing. Let me look at how the grader works — find the grader script.\n\nLet me look at a trial's grader directory and the harness scripts that drive this.\n\nActually, let me step back and check the digest of base test files vs manifest. That determines whether the base checkout = the frozen reference tests."}}
