s>` and each file exists.\n- includes `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts`, `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts` (which the agent must create? or are they restored by grader?)\n\nHmm. Are `tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts` and `tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts` in hiddenTestPaths? Looking at manifest.hiddenTestPaths for the whole suite — the list I printed did NOT include cross-area-composition.test.ts or a5-deep.test.ts. Let me re-check: the hiddenTestPaths list contains 66 entries across all tasks and includes \"openclaw_runtime/src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-budget-shadow.test.ts\", \"openclaw_runtime/packages/agent-core/src/harness/compaction/compression-planner.test.ts\", \"openclaw_runtime/src/context-engine/context-orchestrator.test.ts\", \"openclaw_runtime/src/agents/agent-hooks/compaction-promotion.test.ts\", \"tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts\". So they're all in hiddenTestPaths (the pool). But per-task testPaths for tf-0297-a05 are the 9 listed: resource-aware-wave-scheduler, performance-budgets, deprecation-counters, runtime deprecation-counters, compaction-budget-shadow, compression-planner, context-orchestrator, compaction-promotion, a05-a5-gate-coverage.\n\ncross-area-composition.test.ts and a5-deep.test.ts are NOT in tf-0297-a05's testPaths. They're in the A02/A06 task's scope. Hmm, but the canonical a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts (74da) requires them to EXIST:\n```\nexpect(existsSync(path.join(ROOT, rel))).toBe(true);\n```\nfor rel including \"tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts\" and \"tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts\".\n\nBut in this baseline-2 workspace, those files don't exist and the agent can't rely on the oracle to restore them (they're not in the task's testPaths → they get scrubbed... no wait, scrubbing only removes files in the task's testPaths? Let me reconsider).\n\nActually, look at A01's historical-result: scrubbedOraclePaths = 6 paths (5 preexisting + ... hmm it lists tool-registration, policy-light-snapshott