matches 74da2d9ec and 96afc2c AND 47388bf... let me check. Earlier output: \"MATCH tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts => 74da2d9ec,96afc2c75f899b100d580d1b02ec044c411cd662,65005caf4\". And 47388bf's version was DIFF. Hmm wait, the first scan said 47388bf's a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts DIFF. Let me recheck: in \"d2.cjs\" output (revs list included 47388bf and fd04f0b): a05-a5-gate-coverage MATCH at 74da2d9ec, 96afc2c, 65005caf4. Not 47388bf.\n\nHmm, but 47388bf is the reference commit recorded in the manifest as `referenceCommit`. And its a05-a5-gate-coverage content I printed earlier (via `git show 47388bf...`) was the NO-GO variant:\n\n```\n  it(\"keeps the unresolved resume re-planning criterion explicit as a NO-GO\", () => {\n    ... not.toContain(\"replanOnResume\") ...\n```\n\nWait no — that was the output of `git show 47388bf320000a203b096992c9ddb8a3b2bca487:tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts`. Yes! That's the NO-GO variant. And the second time I printed `96afc2c:...` I got the \"pins the resume re-planning implementation\" variant (the GO variant).\n\nSo there are two variants of a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts:\n- NO-GO variant (47388bf, digest `0e3bdd75...`?) \n- GO variant (96afc2c/74da2d9ec)\n\nThe manifest pins digest 0e3bdd7526b9c409ac1c36197ece1ce996288f1b348731a1769809b1f9780dc5. Let me determine which variant that is.\n\nFrom d2.cjs: `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts` MATCH at 74da2d9ec, 96afc2c, 65005caf4. Those are the GO variant revisions. Hmm, and 47388bf was NOT in that MATCH list, so 47388bf = NO-GO variant = different digest.\n\nBut wait — the manifest says referenceCommit = 47388bf, historicalDecision = \"PASS\". And successState requires `frozenTestsUnchanged: true`. Hmm, but also the manifest's pinned input digests are for files at the candidate commit 96afc2c (the corpus candidate). So the expected final test content = the GO variant (96afc2c).\n\nHold on, that's contradictory with the reference commit being 47388bf and the historicalDecision PASS. Let me look at the a05-acceptance.json at 47388bf vs 74da2d9ec.\n\nActually — the record digest is 4cec9973... which matched 74da2d9ec, 96afc2c, 65005caf4 (and 47388bf was ABSENT for a05-acceptance.json). So the canonical a05-acceptance.json lives at the 65005caf4/96afc2c/74da line, and it says PASS (historicalDecision PASS). That's the post-restoration state (commit 65005caf4 \"close TF-0264 residuals — restore A2/A4/A5/A6 implementations\" restored cross-area-facades, cross-area-composition.test.ts, a5-deep.test.ts).\n\nSo the intended final state for A05 = the state at 74da2d9ec (or 96afc2c / 65005caf4), which:\n- has `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` (238 lines) with ContextBudgetPlanner + replanOnResume\n- has tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts (379 lines)\n- has tests/unit/deep/a5-deep.test.ts (289 lines)\n- a5 spec requiredTests includes the 11 (incl. cross-area-composition.test.ts and a5-deep.test.ts)\n- a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts = GO variant\n\nWait, but then the a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts GO variant is itself a hidden oracle test (hiddenSignalPaths), restored by the grader. So the agent doesn't write it. But the agent's `requiredTests` in the spec must match, and the agent must create cross-area-composition.test.ts and a5-deep.test.ts? Those two are NOT in the tf-0297-a05 task's testPaths and not in preexistingGuardPaths. Are they in hiddenTestPaths (the overall pool)? Let me grep the manifest hiddenTestPaths for those.\n\nEarlier I printed the manifest's hiddenTestPaths list (66 entries). Let me check whether cross-area-composition.test.ts and a5-deep.test.ts are in that list. Scanning... the list includes: agent-dev-reliability-aggregation, agent-dev-paired-ablation, runtime-memory-paired-ablation, error-recovery-next-action, error-governance-boundary, spec-doc-gardening, trace-to-eval-sample, task-ledger-working-context-single-source, context-control-plane-stage3-contracts, context-pressur