rdinator, ResumeContractVerifier\n- orchestration-protocol: OrchestrationTaskGraph\n\nAll exist except cross-area-facades → I create it.\n\nAnd cross-area-facades imports:\n- runtime-core/resume-shadow.js → exists (runRuntimeResumeShadow, RuntimeResumeShadowResult, RuntimeResumeShadowInput)\n- resource-aware-wave-scheduler.js → exists (ResourceAwareWaveScheduler, RePlanRequest, RePlanResult, WavePlan)\n- orchestration-protocol.js → exists\n\nGood.\n\nNow, is the canonical cross-area-facades.ts's `verify()` compatible with the restored performance test? Test: `verifier.verify({ config: undefined }, cycle % 2 === 0)` expects `contract.requiresReverification` toBe(false). With config undefined → resolveRuntimeEventLogFeatureFlags(undefined).resumeReplayShadow. Need to confirm false. If false → enabled false → requiresReverification = (rollback && false) = false. Good. But if it were true, enabled true and rollbackOccurred true on even cycles → requiresReverification true → test fails. Let me verify the flag default.\n\nLet me check event-log.ts resolveRuntimeEventLogFeatureFlags.\n\nAlso note: the canonical facades file has a comment \"// See: net use/designs/...\" which looks like a corrupted path (originally likely \"docs/runtime-design/\"). That's in the reference; harmless.\n\nNow about the coverage guard: The GO a05 gate test also checks `expect(spec).toContain(\"ContextBudgetPlanner.replanOnResume\")`. The base spec already contains \"- `ContextBudgetPlanner.replanOnResume` re-executes on resume, not stale (criterion 3.6)\" → contains \"ContextBudgetPlanner.replanOnResume\". Good.\n\nNow let's determine if any production change to context-orchestrator.ts is needed for the restored context-orchestrator.test.ts.\n\nLet me diff.\n\nLet me run the diff for context-orchestrator.test.ts base vs 74da, and look at what it needs.\n\nLet me proceed with commands. I'll also verify the resume-shadow flag default.\n\nLet me be efficient and batch.\n\nOne more consideration: t