replanOnResume, hasReexecuted, resumeReexecutions), ResumeContractVerifier, FingerprintLeaseCoordinator. ← This makes performance-budgets.test.ts (pinned) pass.\n2. `harness/specs/tasks/a5-adaptive-context-budget-pilot.md` contains the requiredTests entries and re-verification note (so a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts passes).\n3. The reverify spec + docs artifacts exist (acceptance.json, gate.md, SHA256SUMS).\n4. runtime tests pass unchanged — meaning I must NOT break anything.\n\nBut #4 requires the workspace production code to already satisfy those pinned tests. Since the workspace == fd04 (base) and the pinned tests match the *later lineage*, there's risk. But actually, maybe the pinned tests = the versions at the point where A05 was done... no.\n\nHmm, let me look at this from a different angle: check whether the *base sibling* (fd04 checkout) files for these test files match the pinned digests. Earlier digest check on `base\\` (the trial's base dir):\n- MISSING harness.../harness-gap-a05-...reverify.md (expected, it's the new file)\n- MATCH resource-aware-wave-scheduler.test.ts\n- DIFF performance-budgets.test.ts\n- MATCH deprecation-counters.test.ts\n- MATCH observability/deprecation-counters.test.ts\n- MATCH compaction-budget-shadow.test.ts\n- MATCH compression-planner.test.ts\n- DIFF context-orchestrator.test.ts\n- MATCH compaction-promotion.test.ts\n- MISSING a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts (expected)\n\nSo only performance-budgets.test.ts and context-orchestrator.test.ts differ between the fd04 base and the pinned candidate. And those two DIFFs are exactly the ones the A05 reference solution changed (performance-budgets.test.ts: A05 reference added the A6 pause/resume block; context-orchestrator.test.ts: hmm).\n\nWait: performance-budgets.test.ts at 47388 (A05 reference commit on top of fd04) = a27fb409... and pinned = 4502f116 (lf-normalized). Let me check: is the pinned performance-budgets.test.ts (4502f116) the LF-normalized version of the 47388 file? Earlier