{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_312","type":"reasoning","text":"So the manifest input digests correspond to the source-record versions (the corpus was sealed at 96afc2c7 / 74da2d9ec). But the agent's working tree corresponds to fd04f0b4 (the base commit). So there's a mismatch between the \"sealed corpus\" digests (recorded at sealing time from the reference commits) and the agent's base commit. But wait — the manifest's inputDigests is what the *oracle* uses at grading time? Let's look more carefully.\n\nActually the manifest `inputDigests` documents the digests of inputs at the reference revision (the corpus owner's record). The grader restores hidden test files. The question is what version of the hidden test files the grader restores and runs.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The A01 trial: the agent's tree corresponds to base commit a01base = 72ba3c32? No — the a01 trial's agent tree context-orchestrator.test.ts matched \"a01base\" = 72ba3c32. And the baseCommit for tf-0293-a01 is 72ba3c32 (from its historical-result.json). And the grader restored the oracle test files (performance-budgets, deprecation-counters) from... let me check: in the grader directory, performance-budgets.test.ts hash was 585be3c6 (raw). And the A01 manifest inputDigest for performance-budgets is 4502f116... (which is the LF-normalized 585be3c6). So the digest in the manifest is computed with LF normalization, and the file content matches 585be3c6 raw.\n\nHmm wait, 585be3c6 is the *base* version (base commit fd04f0b4 has performance-budgets = a27fb40... no). Let me recheck: base commit fd04f0b4 performance-budgets = a27fb409 (3483 bytes, raw SHA matches inputDigest?), agent workspace = a27fb409. The A05 reference 74da2d9e = 585be3c6 (6050 bytes). But the manifest inputDigest for A05's performance-budgets = 4502f116 which is the LF-normalized form of 585be3c6.\n\nAnd in the A01 trial grader, the restored performance-budgets.test.ts = 585be3c6 raw (6050 bytes). So the hidden test version restored by the grader for A01 is the *reference/enriched* version (6050 bytes with context-budget imports), NOT the base version (3483 bytes).\n\nInteresting! So the grader for A01 restores the enriched performance-budgets.test.ts that imports `ContextBudgetPlanner` from cross-area-facades. Hmm, but that reference version at 74da2d9e requires cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts which does NOT exist in base fd04f0b4. Let me check whether the a01 trial's grader run passed those tests... From the oracle receipt: \"performance-budgets.test.ts (0 test)\" — it failed to even collect (0 test), because the import failed! Indeed the oracle stdout showed `tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts (0 test)`. So the A01 trial's oracle FAILED (verdict=fail). That's expected — A01 baseline trials mostly failed.\n\nHmm OK. So this is a research scenario (RSI) where the \"baseline\" arm agents typically fail, and the task is to figure out what's needed.\n\nWait, but actually let me reconsider. The A05 manifest digests: most match 74da2d9e (the reference solution revision) except:\n- performance-budgets.test.ts: matches 585be3c6 = 74da2d9e version (LF-normalized 4502f116). Wait no: the d2.cjs output said \"NONE tests/unit/performance-budgets.test.ts\" when comparing raw. But d6 showed LF-normalization gives 4502f116 for the grader's 585be3c6 file. So the manifest digest for performance-budgets corresponds to the 74da2d9e/96afc2c7 version.\n\nSo the A05 task's hidden/preexisting test files are the *reference* versions (post-fix), i.e. they will be restored by the grader at grading time. That means the agent doesn't need to create them (they're hidden oracle). But the agent DOES need to create:\n1. `openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts` (production code the hidden tests import)\n2. `harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-a05-adaptive-context-budget-pilot-reverify.md`\n3. `tests/unit/a05-a5-gate-coverage.test.ts` (this is a hiddenSignalPath — the oracle owns it; it